    "intro_html":  "Irish beef stew goes darker and maltier than the American version, and bacon is why. A pound of it renders into the pot before the beef ever hits, and everything that follows tastes like it. The stout is the traditional finish and the one thing we do not price on our grocery board, so treat it as optional. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
